**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests`

**How to implement.** What travels when a kit is sent, as pure Domain data (001 §H 'Send kit… writes one <kit name>.zip (excluding .oc/ and sendExclude)'; 001 §E 'Large lab files (e.g. 24 MB DNG images) may stay in the kit … Send kit… honours sendExclude (e.g. **/*.dng)'; 001 §A '.oc/ app-owned cache and lock; safe to delete; never sent'; the S6 brief: the globs use a small pure matcher in Domain supporting **, * and ?, and no package is added, because STL pins no globbing package). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6, and every type follows `AGENTS.md` (single-case unions carry `.value`, case names have two words, no `bool`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`. (a) Directly before `KitRelativePath` (step 123): `KitPathRole` = `KitAppCachePath` (the path is the app's cache folder or lies under it) | `KitContentPath` (any other path). (b) `KitRelativePath` gains: `static member appCacheFolder : KitRelativePath`, the text `.oc`, the app-owned cache and lock folder (001 §A); `member this.pathRole : KitPathRole`, `KitAppCachePath` when the path's first `/`-separated segment equals `appCacheFolder`'s text ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`); `member this.parentOpt : KitRelativePath option`, the text before the last `/`, `None` for a path at the kit root; and `member this.leafName : FileName`, the text after the last `/` (the whole text at the root). (c) The lock names its folder through `appCacheFolder`: the lock path of `KitFolderStore.fs` (step 129) and the `.oc` and `.oc/lock` entries of `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 129, `KitFolders.fs`), so the text `.oc` is written once in product code. Every answer of those members is unchanged. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs`: `module KitArchive` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `KitHistory.fs` (step 164): one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. It opens `Kit`, `LibraryEntryFiles` (step 24: `FileStem`) and `Softellect.Sys.Primitives`. In this order: (a) `GlobPathMatch` = `GlobPathMatched` | `GlobPathUnmatched`. (b) `type SendExcludeGlob with member this.matchOf (path : KitRelativePath) : GlobPathMatch`, the one glob matcher (`SendExcludeGlob`, step 122). The glob's `\` become `/`, and the glob and the path are split at `/` into segments. A glob segment `**` matches zero or more whole path segments. In any other glob segment `*` matches zero or more characters and `?` exactly one character, never across a `/`, and every other character matches itself ignoring case (the Windows rule `copyTargetFor` follows, step 132). A glob matches the whole path from the kit root: `**/*.dng` matches `IMG_0001.DNG` and `data/raw/a.dng`; `data/raw/big/**` matches everything under `data/raw/big` but not that folder; `*.csv` matches `run.csv` but not `data/run.csv`. It is a recursive match over the two segment lists and, inside a segment, over the two character lists; no regular expression, brace, character class or negation is added. (c) `KitSendChoice` = `SentWithKit` | `LeftOutOfSend`. (d) `KitTreeEntry` = `KitTreeFile of KitRelativePath` | `KitTreeFolder of KitRelativePath`, one file or folder under a kit, with `member this.path : KitRelativePath`. (e) `type KitFile with member this.sendChoiceOf (path : KitRelativePath) : KitSendChoice` answers `LeftOutOfSend` for a `KitAppCachePath` path and for a path that, or any folder holding it (its chain of `parentOpt`), a glob of `sendExclude` answers `GlobPathMatched`; `SentWithKit` otherwise. So a glob that names a folder leaves out the folder and everything in it. `member this.sentEntries (tree : KitTreeEntry list) : KitTreeEntry list` keeps, in order, the entries whose path is `SentWithKit`. (f) `type KitName with member this.zipFileName : FileName` is `this.fileStem.withExtension (FileExtension ".zip")` (steps 24, 122): the one place `.zip` is written, so a kit named `Optics: QZ/LR` is sent as `Optics_ QZ_LR.zip`. No other type, member or option is added; S8.3's naming template and S9.2's import profiles add nothing here. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs`, `module KitArchiveTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment; every path is made through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate`. `a glob matches whole segments with a double star, and characters with star and question mark inside one segment, ignoring case`: `**/*.dng` matches `IMG_0001.DNG`, `data/raw/a.dng` and `data/a.Dng`, and not `data/a.dngx`; `data/raw/big/**` matches `data/raw/big/x.dng` and `data/raw/big/y/z.csv`, and not `data/raw/big` or `data/raw/bigger/x`; `*.csv` matches `run.csv` and not `data/run.csv`; `data/run ?.csv` matches `data/run 1.csv` and not `data/run 10.csv`; `data\raw\*.csv` matches `data/raw/a.csv`; `**` matches `.kit-json` and `data/raw/a.csv`. `the app cache is never sent, and a glob leaves out what it matches and everything inside a folder it matches`: over a kit file whose `sendExclude` is `**/*.dng` and `data/scratch`, `.oc`, `.oc/lock` and `.OC/planner/x.json` are `LeftOutOfSend`; so are `data/raw/IMG_0001.DNG`, `data/scratch` and `data/scratch/a.csv`; `.kit-json`, `data`, `data/raw`, `data/run 1.csv`, `library/x.material-json` and `.ocx/a` are `SentWithKit`. `the sent entries keep the tree's order and drop what is left out` : a tree, in ordinal order, of the folders `.oc`, `data`, `data/raw` and `library` and the files `.kit-json`, `.oc/lock`, `data/raw/IMG_0001.DNG`, `data/run 1.csv` and `notes.txt` answers, under the glob `**/*.dng`, every entry but `.oc`, `.oc/lock` and the DNG, in the tree's order; with no glob it answers every entry but `.oc` and `.oc/lock`. `a kit is sent as a zip named for it`: `(KitName "Optics: QZ/LR").zipFileName` is `FileName "Optics_ QZ_LR.zip"`. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `a kit path knows its folder, its leaf and whether it is the app's cache`: `data/raw/run 1.csv` has `parentOpt` `Some data/raw`, `leafName` `FileName "run 1.csv"` and `KitContentPath`; `.kit-json` has `parentOpt` `None` and `leafName` `FileName ".kit-json"`; `appCacheFolder` is `.oc` and `KitAppCachePath`; `.oc/lock` is `KitAppCachePath` and `.ocx` `KitContentPath`.

**Acceptance.** After the send rule lands, `SendExcludeGlob.matchOf` MUST match `**`, `*` and `?` as specified, `KitFile.sendChoiceOf` MUST leave out the app cache and every path a glob or a matched folder covers, and the lock MUST name `.oc` through `KitRelativePath.appCacheFolder`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a glob matches whole segments with a double star, and characters with star and question mark inside one segment, ignoring case`, `the app cache is never sent, and a glob leaves out what it matches and everything inside a folder it matches`, `the sent entries keep the tree's order and drop what is left out`, `a kit is sent as a zip named for it` and `a kit path knows its folder, its leaf and whether it is the app's cache`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
